So the rule is specifically about special bits with `+`/`-`: they only work after a `=`.

Let me formalize the algorithm:

```
mode = 0755  // starting mode
seen_equals = false

for each clause in mode_string (comma-separated):
    parse who, op, perms
    
    if op == '=':
        seen_equals = true
        // Handle ordinary bits
        if who is explicit:
            mode = (mode & ~who_rwx_mask) | (perms_rwx & who_rwx_mask)
        else:
            mode = (mode & ~0777) | (perms_rwx & ~umask)
        // Handle special bits
        // s/t are set if mentioned in perms, cleared if not
        if 's' in perms:
            // set s bits for relevant who
            if who includes u: mode |= 04000
            if who includes g: mode |= 02000
        else:
            // clear s bits? No, "preserve unless explicitly addressed"
            // So if s is NOT in perms, preserve existing s bits
        if 't' in perms:
            mode |= 01000
        else:
            mode &= ~01000  // clear sticky if not mentioned in = clause
    elif op == '+':
        // Ordinary bits
        if who is explicit:
            mode |= (perms_rwx & who_rwx_mask)
        else:
            mode |= (perms_rwx & ~umask)
        // Special bits
        if seen_equals:
            if 's' in perms:
                if who includes u or who is a or who is omitted: mode |= 04000
                if who includes g or who is a or who is omitted: mode |= 02000
            if 't' in perms:
                mode |= 01000
    elif op == '-':
        // Ordinary bits
        if who is explicit:
            mode &= ~(perms_rwx & who_rwx_mask)
        else:
            mode &= ~(perms_rwx & ~umask)
        // Special bits
        if seen_equals:
            if 's' in perms:
                if who includes u or who is a or who is omitted: mode &= ~04000
                if who includes g or who is a or who is omitted: mode &= ~02000
            if 't' in perms:
                mode &= ~01000
```

