- "755" (3 digits) → value 0755, setuid/setgid not specified → inherit
- "0755" (4 digits) → value 0755, setuid/setgid not specified (leading 0) → inherit
- "4755" (4 digits) → value 4755, setuid specified (4), setgid not specified → inherit setgid
- "00755" (5 digits) → value 0755, setuid explicitly cleared (0), setgid explicitly cleared (0)
- "04755" (5 digits) → value 4755, setuid set (4), setgid explicitly cleared (0)

So the rule is based on the LENGTH of the input string:
- ≤4 digits: the special digit (if present, i.e., 4 digits) has 0=inherit, non-zero=set those bits
- ≥5 digits: the special digit has 0=explicitly clear, non-zero=set those bits

